      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to substitute the given values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) into the expression \\(2a + 3b\\). Let's go through the steps in detail:\n\n1. **Identify the given values:**\n   \\[\n   a = 2 - i \\quad \\text{and} \\quad b = -1 + i\n   \\]\n\n2. **Substitute \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) into the expression \\(2a + 3b\\):**\n   \\[\n   2a + 3b = 2(2 - i) + 3(-1 + i)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Distribute the constants 2 and 3:**\n   \\[\n   2(2 - i) = 2 \\cdot 2 - 2 \\cdot i = 4 - 2i\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3(-1 + i) = 3 \\cdot -1 + 3 \\cdot i = -3 + 3i\n   \\]\n\n4. **Combine the results from the distribution:**\n   \\[\n   2(2 - i) + 3(-1 + i) = (4 - 2i) + (-3 + 3i)\n   \\]\n\n5. **Add the real parts and the imaginary parts separately:**\n   \\[\n   (4 - 3) + (-2i + 3i) = 1 + i\n   \\]\n\n6. **Write the final answer:**\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{1 + i}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(2a + 3b\\) where \\(a = 2 - i\\) and \\(b = -1 + i\\) is \\(\\boxed{1 + i}\\).",
